<Base title="About" active="about">
<div class="reading"><p class="eyebrow">A little background</p><div class="about-intro"><div><h1>About me.</h1>
<p class="lead">I’m Jake Baskin, an educator and nonprofit leader in Chicago.</p></div><img class="portrait" src="/images/jake-baskin.png" alt="Jake Baskin" width="954" height="954" decoding="async" /></div>
<p>As Executive Director of the <a href="https://csteachers.org/">Computer Science Teachers Association</a>, I work to make sure every K–12 computer science teacher has a community they can rely on.</p>
<p>I got my start studying computer science at <a href="https://www.swarthmore.edu/">Swarthmore College</a>. I went on to teach high school computer science at <a href="https://www.lindblomeagles.org/">Lindblom Math and Science Academy</a> in Chicago, then worked in outreach and government affairs at <a href="https://code.org/">Code.org</a>.</p>
<p>When it’s warm enough, I like to ride my bike along the lakefront, go to White Sox games, and keep meaning to write more poetry.</p>
<section class="section"><h2>Get in touch.</h2><p>You can find me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jakebaskin/">LinkedIn</a>.</p></section></div>
</Base>

